{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "MosaicMesaPtcStep",
    "description": "One pass of MOSAIC's MESA solid-liquid solver, SUBROUTINE mesa_ptc of chem/module_mosaic_therm.F (WRF v4.8.0) with its callees mesa_flux_salt, mesa_estimate_eleliquid, mesa_dissolve_small_salt, mesa_convergence_criterion and electrolytes_to_ions, for ONE size bin. MESA (Zaveri et al., 2005) decides how much of each soluble salt of a particle above its mutual deliquescence point is solid: aerosol_phase_state.esm hands it the bin (branch 6 of SUBROUTINE mesa) after do_full_deliquescence, and it then moves salt between the solid and the liquid in pseudo-time until either the solid holds 98% of the salt mass (all solid), or every salt's relative driving force is within 1% (all liquid, or mixed), or 80 passes have gone by (mixed).\n\nWHAT A PASS IS. With the solid electrolytes E_s from the previous pass, the liquid is the total less the solid; ions_to_electrolytes.esm forms the liquid electrolytes (moving any new CaSO4 to the solid), aerosol_water_zsr.esm and mtem_activities.esm give the water and the activities, and THIS component does the rest:\n  - saturation S_s = a_s / K_s(T) of each of the fifteen soluble salts (keq_sl by template fn_keq), and the relative driving force phi_s = (S_s - 1)/max(S_s, 1);\n  - a salt that is undersaturated and under 1% of the solid is dissolved outright (mesa_dissolve_small_salt: its ions return to the liquid);\n  - the flux S_s - 1, switched off for an undersaturated salt with no solid, for Ca(NO3)2 and CaCl2 always, and -- when calcium is dissolved -- for a salt under 1% of the liquid electrolytes or absent from the totals;\n  - the convergence tests (mesa_convergence_criterion);\n  - the step: an adaptive fraction alpha_s of the time the salt needs to precipitate the liquid's estimated stock of it (tau_p = eleliquid/|flux|, mesa_estimate_eleliquid) or to dissolve its solid (tau_d), E_s <- E_s + h_s flux_s; then electrolytes_to_ions(jsolid) and the liquid for the next pass.\nThe inputs are the state a pass starts from (E_s, phi_old, alpha) and that pass's ions_to_electrolytes / water / activity results; the outputs are everything the pass decides. Pass number `it` matters only for phi_bar (formed from the second pass on).\n\nWHY THE LOOP IS NOT WRITTEN HERE (and why it is a genuine recurrence). The three CLAUDE.md tests all fail on the pass-to-pass carry: (a) it does not unroll into a reduction of the original values -- every pass reads the previous pass's E_s through the activities; (b) it IS a pseudo-time integration of dE_s/dtau = S(E_s) - 1, but explicit Euler with a different, adaptive step per salt and a stopping rule, so a lowering rule for the ODE would not reproduce the Fortran's answer at its 1% tolerance or at its 80-pass cut-off (206 of the chem170 column's 4074 hand-offs end there); (c) the carry is three coupled quantities (E_s, phi_old, alpha) with no conserved sum to split them -- the conserved sum, solid + liquid = total, is already used to drop the liquid from the state. That is a three-variable cycle, which esm 4.3.1.1 on the pinned be1fafe6d binary forbids (EarthSciAST #701, recurrence groups, PR #703), and each pass also needs ions_to_electrolytes, the ZSR water and the MTEM activities, which are models, not templates. So the pass is a component and the loop an assembly that waits for both; couplings/mosaic_mesa_pass.esm wires ONE pass of the chain together.\n\nFORTRAN NOTES. mesa_estimate_eleliquid's sulfate-poor branch reads nc(jc_h) before setting it (FORTRAN_BUGS B30); in this build it acts as zero, which is what is written here, and the acidic sulfate-poor test pins it. The Fortran's sulfate-rich estimate writes Ca(MSA)2 into the liquid electrolytes rather than into the estimate, so eleliquid of Ca(MSA)2 is zero there. mesa_convergence_criterion leaves iconverge_flux unset on a mass-converged exit; conv_flux is defined as 0 then. If a pass finds no liquid water, mesa_flux_salt returns before recomputing phi, so phi is the previous pass's (phi_in); that branch is never reached by the tests (FORTRAN_BUGS N120 lists these).\n\nPRECISION. Double precision with MOSAIC's default-REAL literals at their binary32 values (mosaic_mesa_parameters.esm). electrolytes_to_ions is written as the stoichiometric sum over electrolytes, not in the Fortran's own order of terms; the two agree within the tests' tolerance, including the next liquid, total minus solid, which can be a small difference (its assertions carry an absolute floor of 1e-12 of the bin's largest total amount).\n\nTESTS: the MESA tape (WRF fork module_esm_mesa_tape at every pass and at mesa_ptc's own exit, kernels/mosaic_therm_driver; data/eqwefic/chem170_scm/mesa64): column hand-offs of the chem170 aerosol_phase_state capture replayed bit for bit (all 4074, verified field by field), plus hand-specified bins for the branches the column never reaches. Real64 at rel 1e-9; flags exactly. Mutations caught (counts of failing assertions): the alpha caps 0.9/0.5 (28, 21), no small-salt dissolution (48), dissolved ions not returned (24), the 1% small-fraction band at 2% (80), the 1e25 no-flux step (395), 298.15 at double rather than binary32 (1037), the two calcium Heaviside conditions (4, 11), phi_bar from the first pass (8), a tau_p = 0 precipitation not stopped (6), rtol 0.02 (4), solid fraction 0.97 (2), the no-salt shortcut (2), the crustal threshold (1), the unclipped charge-balance H+ (1), an H+ of zero in the sulfate-poor estimate (8, i.e. B30's reading), the estimate's split at 1.9999 (2). Not caught: phi_bar's -10 floor (never reached), rtol at 0.0101, 5/3 at double, Ca(MSA)2 in the sulfate-rich estimate (unreachable: calcium leaves as CaSO4 first), and Na3H(SO4)2's activity zeroing (the activity input is recorded after it; no pass has solid Na3H(SO4)2).",
    "authors": [
      "EqWeFiC"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Zaveri, R.A., Easter, R.C., Peters, L.K. (2005). A computationally efficient Multicomponent Equilibrium Solver for Aerosols (MESA). J. Geophys. Res. 110, D24203."
      },
      {
        "citation": "WRF v4.8.0 chem/module_mosaic_therm.F"
      }
    ]
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "salt": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 15
    },
    "sp": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 7
    },
    "el": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 22
    },
    "ion": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 9
    },
    "aer": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 112
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "MosaicMesaPtcStep": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "./mosaic_thermo_templates.esm"
        }
      ],
      "subsystems": {
        "tp": {
          "ref": "./mosaic_thermo_parameters.esm"
        },
        "pp": {
          "ref": "./mosaic_phase_parameters.esm"
        },
        "mp": {
          "ref": "./mosaic_mesa_parameters.esm"
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "it": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "The pseudo-time iteration number itdum (1 on the first pass): phi_bar is only formed from the second pass on."
        },
        "t_k": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K",
          "default": 298.0,
          "description": "Temperature (the model's real32 t_k), for the solid-liquid constants keq_sl."
        },
        "aer_t": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "aer"
          ],
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "The bin's total species aer(:, jtotal), nmol per m3 of air."
        },
        "elec_t": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "el"
          ],
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "The bin's total electrolytes electrolyte(:, jtotal)."
        },
        "elec_s_in": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "el"
          ],
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Solid electrolytes electrolyte(:, jsolid) at the start of the iteration (do_full_deliquescence's CaSO4 and CaCO3 on the first pass, the previous pass's update after)."
        },
        "phi_old_in": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "salt"
          ],
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "phi_salt_old, the relative driving force each salt had on the previous pass."
        },
        "alpha_in": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "salt"
          ],
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "alpha_salt, the step fraction each salt took on the previous pass."
        },
        "phi_in": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "salt"
          ],
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "phi_salt as the previous pass left it: what the module still holds if this pass finds no water (mesa_flux_salt then returns before recomputing it)."
        },
        "a_l": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "sp"
          ],
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "The liquid species after ions_to_electrolytes (ions_to_electrolytes.esm `a`: clipped, CaSO4 removed), `sp` order so4, no3, cl, nh4, msa, na, ca."
        },
        "caso4": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "The CaSO4 ions_to_electrolytes moved from the liquid to the solid on this pass (ions_to_electrolytes.esm `caso4`)."
        },
        "elec_l": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "el"
          ],
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "The liquid electrolytes ions_to_electrolytes formed (ions_to_electrolytes.esm `elec`)."
        },
        "water": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "default": 1e-09,
          "description": "The liquid water compute_activities found for those electrolytes (aerosol_water_zsr.esm at the bin's water activity)."
        },
        "activity": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "el"
          ],
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "The electrolyte activities compute_activities found (mtem_activities.esm `activity`)."
        },
        "elec_t_sum": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "Sum of the total electrolytes."
        },
        "present": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "salt"
          ],
          "description": "jsalt_present: 1 for a salt above 1 mole percent of the total electrolytes."
        },
        "aer_h": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "Charge-balance H+ of the totals, clipped at zero here (mesa_ptc's raz 11/13/2008 update; aerosol_phase_state does not clip it)."
        },
        "mass_dry": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "g/cm^3",
          "description": "mass_dry_a as mesa_ptc recomputes it: (sum of aer_t M + aer_h) 1e-15."
        },
        "mass_dry_salt": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "g/cm^3",
          "description": "Dry mass of the fifteen soluble salts, sum of E_t M 1e-15."
        },
        "keq_sl": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "salt"
          ],
          "description": "Solid-liquid equilibrium constants at t_k (fn_keq; keq_sl of update_thermodynamic_constants)."
        },
        "elec_s0": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "el"
          ],
          "description": "Solid electrolytes once ions_to_electrolytes has added this pass's CaSO4."
        },
        "wet": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "1 when the liquid holds water; with none mesa_flux_salt zeroes every flux and returns."
        },
        "sat0": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "salt"
          ],
          "description": "Saturation ratio of each salt, its activity over keq_sl (Na3H(SO4)2's activity is set to zero first)."
        },
        "elec_l_sum": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "Sum of the liquid electrolytes."
        },
        "frac_l": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "salt"
          ],
          "description": "Mole fraction of each salt among the liquid electrolytes (epercent/100)."
        },
        "solid_sum": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "Sum of the solid salts."
        },
        "frac_s": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "salt"
          ],
          "description": "Fraction of each salt among the solid salts."
        },
        "calcium": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "Dissolved calcium, read before any small salt is dissolved."
        },
        "dissolve": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "salt"
          ],
          "description": "1 for a salt that is undersaturated and under 1% of the solid salts (but present): mesa_dissolve_small_salt returns all of it to the liquid. NH4MSA, NaMSA and Ca(MSA)2 have no branch there and stay."
        },
        "dissolved_el": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "el"
          ],
          "description": "dissolve spread over the electrolyte index (0 for the non-salts)."
        },
        "elec_s1": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "el"
          ],
          "description": "Solid electrolytes after the small salts have dissolved."
        },
        "a_l1": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "sp"
          ],
          "description": "Liquid species after the small salts have dissolved: each returns its ions (tp.stoich mapped onto species by mp.ion_species)."
        },
        "zero_flux": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "salt"
          ],
          "description": "The Heaviside conditions of mesa_flux_salt: an undersaturated salt with no solid to dissolve, or (with calcium dissolved) a salt under 1% of the liquid or absent from the totals; and Ca(NO3)2 and CaCl2 always."
        },
        "flux": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "salt"
          ],
          "description": "flux_sl = S - 1, zero where zero_flux holds or the liquid has no water."
        },
        "phi": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "salt"
          ],
          "description": "Relative driving force phi = (S - 1)/max(S, 1), zero where zero_flux holds; the previous pass's value if the liquid has no water."
        },
        "sat": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "salt"
          ],
          "description": "sat_ratio as the routine leaves it: Ca(NO3)2 and CaCl2 forced to 1."
        },
        "xt_e": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "X_T of the liquid after dissolution."
        },
        "est_poor": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "1 when X_T >= 2 or < 0: the estimate pairs ions by equivalent fractions."
        },
        "n_ion": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "ion"
          ],
          "description": "Ion amounts for the sulfate-poor pairing of the estimate (`ion` order); its H+ is the anion excess."
        },
        "cation_eq": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "Cation charge equivalents of n_ion."
        },
        "anion_eq": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "Anion charge equivalents of n_ion."
        },
        "l_poor": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "el"
          ],
          "description": "Sulfate-poor estimate: every pair by equivalent fractions (template ion_pair_electrolyte)."
        },
        "camsa_e": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "Ca(MSA)2 the sulfate-rich estimate sets aside (form_camsa2; it is written to the liquid electrolytes, not to the estimate)."
        },
        "msa_re": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "MSA left after it."
        },
        "nanh4_e": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "Na + NH4 of the liquid."
        },
        "f_nh4_e": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Ammonium share of Na + NH4."
        },
        "f_na_e": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Sodium share of Na + NH4."
        },
        "msa_short_e": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "1 when Na + NH4 exceed the remaining MSA."
        },
        "l_nh4msa": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "Estimated NH4MSA."
        },
        "l_namsa": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "Estimated NaMSA."
        },
        "l_msa": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "Estimated free MSA."
        },
        "xna": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "1 + Na/(2 SO4): the X_T at which sodium alone would neutralise the sulfate to Na2SO4 on top of bisulfate."
        },
        "xdum": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "SO4 - NH4."
        },
        "xnh4": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "2 NH4/(2 SO4 - Na), ammonium per sulfate left after sodium (0 without ammonium or with sodium beyond 2 SO4)."
        },
        "l_na2so4": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "Estimated Na2SO4 in the sulfate-rich domain."
        },
        "l_nahso4": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "Estimated NaHSO4."
        },
        "l_nh4so4": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "Estimated (NH4)2SO4."
        },
        "l_lvc": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "Estimated letovicite."
        },
        "l_nh4hso4": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "Estimated NH4HSO4."
        },
        "eleliquid": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "el"
          ],
          "description": "mesa_estimate_eleliquid: the amount of each electrolyte the liquid could hold, the scale of the precipitation time."
        },
        "mass_solid_salt": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "g/cm^3",
          "description": "Mass of the solid salts."
        },
        "conv_mass": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Mass convergence: no salt at all (below 1e-30 g/cm3), or the solid salts hold 98% of the salt mass. mesa_ptc then calls the bin all solid."
        },
        "conv_flux": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Flux convergence (only tested without mass convergence): every |phi| within rtol."
        },
        "sumflux": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Sum of |flux|."
        },
        "crustal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "ng/m^3",
          "description": "Crustal solids, CaCO3 + CaSO4 + OIN by mass (xhyst_up_crustal_thresh, 2017.12.03)."
        },
        "dissolved": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "1 when the fluxes have converged with no flux at all and the crustal solids are at most 30% of the dry mass: the bin is all liquid rather than mixed."
        },
        "outcome": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "0 carry on, 1 mass-converged (all solid), 2 flux-converged (all liquid if dissolved, else mixed)."
        },
        "elec_s_exit": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "el"
          ],
          "description": "On a flux-converged exit the solid electrolytes, negatives removed."
        },
        "phi_bar_raw": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Change of |phi| per unit alpha over the last pass, (|phi| - |phi_old|)/alpha_old, when phi kept its sign (and from the second pass); 0 otherwise (oscillating, or a zero).",
          "shape": [
            "salt"
          ]
        },
        "phi_bar": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "salt"
          ],
          "description": "phi_bar with a falling value floored at -10 (what the module keeps)."
        },
        "alpha": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "salt"
          ],
          "description": "Step fraction: 3 exp(phi_bar) |phi| capped at 0.9 while |phi| falls, |phi| capped at 0.5 while it grows, |phi|/3 capped at 0.5 when it oscillates."
        },
        "tau_p": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "Precipitation scale eleliquid/|flux|.",
          "shape": [
            "salt"
          ]
        },
        "tau_d": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "Dissolution scale E_solid/|flux| of a dissolving salt.",
          "shape": [
            "salt"
          ]
        },
        "hsalt": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "salt"
          ],
          "description": "Pseudo-time step of each salt: alpha tau_p when precipitating, alpha min(tau_p, tau_d) when dissolving (alpha tau_d if tau_p = 0), 1e25 with no flux or a zero precipitation scale."
        },
        "flux_out": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "salt"
          ],
          "description": "flux_sl after the step: a precipitating salt with nothing to precipitate (tau_p = 0) is stopped."
        },
        "phi_out": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "salt"
          ],
          "description": "phi_salt after the step (zeroed with flux_out). The next pass's phi_old is phi, taken before this zeroing."
        },
        "elec_s_new": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "el"
          ],
          "description": "Solid electrolytes after the step, E_s + hsalt flux."
        },
        "a_s_new": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "sp"
          ],
          "description": "Solid species from them (electrolytes_to_ions(jsolid)): each electrolyte's ions (tp.stoich) mapped onto MOSAIC's species (mp.ion_species: HSO4- and SO4-- are both so4). HHSO4 is never solid; CaCO3's carbonate is not one of the `sp` species."
        },
        "a_t": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "sp"
          ],
          "description": "Total species in the `sp` order."
        },
        "a_l_new": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "sp"
          ],
          "description": "Liquid species for the next pass, total minus solid."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": "elec_t_sum",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "faq",
            "output_idx": [],
            "reduce": "+",
            "args": [],
            "ranges": {
              "e": {
                "from": "el"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "index",
              "args": [
                "elec_t",
                "e"
              ]
            }
          }
