        {
          "id": "hand_split_band_m5_c1_it1",
          "description": "Covers: est_split_band. Source: hand-specified bin 'split_band_m5' (X_T = 1.999925, between ions_to_electrolytes' 1.9999 split (sulfate-poor there) and the estimate's 2 (sulfate-rich there); electrolytes given (mode 5) as letovicite + ammonium sulfate; chem170_scm/mesa64/make_mesa_hand.py), mesa_ptc call 1, pass 1. Inputs: the pass's starting state (TOP record) and its ions_to_electrolytes / water / activity results (THERM record); expected: the FLUX record (after mesa_convergence_criterion), the STEP record (after the step, when the pass does not exit) or the EXIT record (solid electrolytes on a flux-converged exit), and keq_sl / jsalt_present / dry masses from the ENTRY record. Real64 MESA tape (WRF's own compiled mesa_ptc via kernels/mosaic_therm_driver, WRF fork earthsciml-instrumented-chem170); rel 1e-9, amounts with an absolute floor of 1e-12 of the bin's largest total species amount (the round-off of a total-minus-solid difference), flags exactly.",
